#heading([Abstract])

Zoology teaching is essential for training in biological and environmental sciences. This study analyzed the contributions of the Educa Serpentes project to the conceptual and attitudinal profile of Ecology students at the Federal University of Paraíba (Campus IV – Rio Tinto). The research involved 60 first-year students who participated in theoretical-practical activities and educational games. Data were collected through pre- and post-intervention questionnaires and analyzed using descriptive statistics. The results indicated advances in conceptual understanding and in the perception of the ecological importance of snakes. It is concluded that educational interventions contribute to scientific literacy and the demystification of these animals.

Keywords: Conservation; Environmental Education; Herpetofauna; Ludic Activities; Zoology Teaching.
